add('UA','conditional','Legal classification inference: the import phytosanitary list approved by Resolution 1177/2019 omits ordinary tea (HS 0902), while expressly listing other plant foods including raw coffee and mate. Ukraine Customs separately allows food in international personal post up to 10 kg in the manufacturer’s packaging.','The Customs guidance expressly identifies international postal and express consignments to citizens. Its 10 kg allowance is distinct from passenger food limits.','Ukraine Customs; Cabinet of Ministers Resolution 1177/2019',['https://customs.gov.ua/news/zagalne-20/post/korisna-informatsiia-pravila-vvezennia-produktiv-kharchuvannia-v-ukrayinu-1846','https://zakon.rada.gov.ua/laws/show/1177-2019-%D0%BF','https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/ukr194178.pdf'],limit={'netGrams':10000,'inclusive':True,'scope':'Food in a personal international postal or express consignment, in manufacturer packaging; this is a postal food allowance, not a phytosanitary tea threshold.'},attempts=['Read the full import phytosanitary list under Resolution 1177/2019, which replaced Resolution 705/2007; ordinary tea HS 0902 is absent, while coffee 0901 and mate 0903 appear.','Read Customs’ explicit postal food exception under Customs Code Article 378; excluded the separate passenger 2 kg/product allowance.'])
add('ZA','permit_required','Legal inference from the current Agricultural Pests Act: its definition of plant includes dead parts and derivatives, and section 3 requires an import permit unless an exemption applies. The complete R1013 exemption table, consolidated through 2022, lists food herbs by genus but contains no Camellia/Thea exemption. Treat manufactured sencha as requiring a plant import permit; obtain the consignment’s certificate and inspection conditions through that permit.','The Act applies to imports by any person and does not create a general small personal-post exemption. A permit route is not evidence that the recipient already holds a permit or that a particular application will be approved.','South African Department of Agriculture; Agricultural Pests Act 36/1983 and Regulations R1013/1989; current consolidation hosted by Germany’s NPPO',['https://www.nda.gov.za/images/Services/Agricultural%20Pests%20Act.pdf','https://pflanzengesundheit.julius-kuehn.de/dokumente/upload/za_1989-1013cons2022-2855_einfuhr_de.pdf','https://www.nda.gov.za/component/content/article/299-import-authorisation?Itemid=437&catid=19','https://www.gov.za/documents/acts/plant-health-phytosanitary-act-35-2024-20-dec-2024'],question='Confirm with the permit office whether it has a separate processing-specific dispensation for commercially steamed/dried retail Camellia sinensis tea; none was found in the published statutory exemption table. The issued permit must establish the required Japanese phytosanitary documentation.',attempts=['Read the Act’s plant definition and section 3 default import-permit rule.','Checked every genus in the complete R1013 food-herb exemption table, including C and T; no Camellia or Thea entry occurs.','Verified that the replacement Plant Health Act 35/2024 is still listed by government as awaiting commencement; did not treat the 2025 draft import regulations as enacted.'])
add('AD','not_verified','Andorra’s phytosanitary regulation controls relevant plants and plant products; no affirmative finished-tea exemption or personal postal allowance was verified for steamed/dried Japanese sencha. A rule concerning living plants or fresh material alone cannot settle this product.','The available phytosanitary regulation is general import law; no personal postal provision resolving finished dried tea was found.','Andorra official legal portal, 2013 phytosanitary regulation and 2021 annex amendment',['https://www.portaljuridicandorra.ad/R20130612A_1','https://www.portaljuridicandorra.ad/R20210203A'],question='Does commercially steamed/dried Camellia sinensis tea fall outside the regulated plant-product definition for a private postal import from Japan, or is a phytosanitary certificate required?',attempts=['Read the plant-product definitions and certificate annex in the official phytosanitary regulation.','Searched Andorran agriculture and customs guidance for tea and private postal imports; did not establish a finished-tea exception.'])
add('AL','not_verified','The currently applicable Albanian plant-protection framework requires controls on regulated plant products. No current product-specific determination or personal-post exemption was verified for sealed manufactured Japanese tea.','A passenger small-quantity allowance, if applicable to living plants, does not establish an exemption for this online postal purchase.','Albanian plant-protection framework; official CEFTA trade portal; European Commission legislative status report',['https://leap.unep.org/en/countries/al/national-legislation/law-no-1052016-plant-protection','https://transparency.cefta.int/TradePortal?articleId=358&id=3&lid=5&pid=2','https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/ALL/?uri=CELEX%3A52025SC0750'],question='Does the authority classify HS 090210 manufactured sencha as requiring phytosanitary inspection or certification under the currently applicable law, and is there a personal postal exemption?',attempts=['Checked Law 105/2016 and the trade portal’s import-control description.','Checked the 2025 EU report: new Law 40/2025 does not apply until June 2027, so its future EU alignment cannot establish today’s exemption.','Searched for a tea-specific current rule and postal personal-use exemption without finding an authoritative determination.'])
add('GI','not_verified','Gibraltar’s current import-control framework was located, but no affirmative determination of agricultural admissibility for a private postal consignment of manufactured Japanese tea was verified.','Postal restrictions mention plant and food imports, but do not distinguish this finished tea from regulated plant commodities or commercial food consignments.','Gibraltar Laws; Gibraltar postal country return supplied to the UPU',['https://www.gibraltarlaws.gov.gi/legislations/imports-and-exports-control-regulations-1987-425','https://guypost.gy/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/ListOfProhibitedArticles-updated.pdf'],question='Is sealed manufactured Camellia sinensis tea bought by an individual through the post exempt from plant-health certificates or import permissions under current Gibraltar law?',attempts=['Located the July 2026 consolidation of the Imports and Exports (Control) Regulations 1987 and the Gibraltar postal country return.','Searched Gibraltar government guidance for tea, plant products and personal postal imports; no affirmative tea determination found.','Did not apply the draft UK–EU Gibraltar treaty as current law.'])
add('RS','not_verified','Serbian Customs’ plant-health control list effective 1 January 2026 expressly includes HS 090210 and other green/black tea codes, including retail packs. The published small-quantity plant exemption is for natural persons entering Serbia with specified European-origin material; it does not establish an exemption for Japanese tea sent by post.','The current customs list establishes phytosanitary control, but does not by itself resolve whether this personal postal pouch needs a Japanese phytosanitary certificate or only arrival inspection.','Serbian Customs; Plant Health Law; 2011 small-quantity plant rule',['https://www.carina.rs/upload/media/2025/12/31/66788/%D0%A4%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%BE-%D0%B1%D0%B8%D1%99%D0%B5_01_01_2026.pdf','https://pflanzengesundheit.julius-kuehn.de/index.php?downloadid=1052&menuid=28&reporeid=126','https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/srb161040.pdf'],question='For a private postal shipment of 100 g manufactured Japanese green tea under HS 090210, does Serbia require a phytosanitary certificate from Japan, or only inspection at the postal import point?',attempts=['Read the current Customs plant-health commodity list and confirmed ordinary tea HS 0902 is included.','Read Plant Health Law Articles 70–71 and the complete small-quantity implementing rule: it concerns entry by natural persons, European-origin products and specified quantities, without a finished-tea postal exception.','Searched for the current certificate schedule applicable to manufactured tea; did not verify whether the certificate or inspection-only route applies.'])
add('VA','not_verified','No Vatican-specific agricultural import rule confirming admission of finished dried tea in personal post was located. Its postal service documentation alone does not establish a phytosanitary exemption.','Postal documentation confirms the service, but the material found did not address inbound personal tea consignments or identify the agricultural clearance rule.','Vatican postal service; Vatican postal country return supplied to the UPU',['https://www.postevaticane.va/script-php/poste/PHPposte-invioPacchi/index.php','https://guypost.gy/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/ListOfProhibitedArticles-updated.pdf'],question='Which Vatican or Italian agricultural entry rule applies to a Japanese tea parcel addressed to a Vatican individual, and does finished retail tea require any plant-health permission?',attempts=['Checked Vatican postal customs guidance and the destination’s UPU country return.','Searched for applicable Vatican plant-health legislation or an agreement applying Italy’s dried-tea exemption; no authoritative link was established.'])
add('XK','not_verified','Kosovo’s published cargo rules require Food and Veterinary Agency clearance for tariff products assigned plant-control measures. The material reviewed did not establish whether manufactured retail tea HS 090210 has a FIT measure or a personal postal exemption.','The 1 kg personal-food exemption in the cargo guidance concerns veterinary goods, so it cannot be used as a plant-health exemption for tea.','Kosovo Air Navigation Services official AIP; Kosovo Food and Veterinary Agency and Customs',['https://kans-ks.org/eAIP/AIP%20AMDT%2001-2024_2024_12_26/eAIP/BK-GEN%201.4-en-GB.html','https://auvk.rks-gov.net/','https://dogana.rks-gov.net/Individs'],question='Does Kosovo’s current TARIK assign FIT/L02 plant clearance to sealed Japanese green tea HS 090210, and is any certificate or inspection waived for a 100 g personal postal purchase?',attempts=['Read the AIP cargo phytosanitary and veterinary provisions and distinguished their different exemptions.','Checked Customs personal-import guidance and searched the FVA site; no finished-tea postal exception or current commodity clearance determination was verified.'])
